  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The model–WOA23 correlation, RMSE and differences must be computed only where both fields have data, using one common mask rather than WOA23's land-sea mask applied to non-WOA sources.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build one shared valid-data mask over all four nitracline fields with `build_comparison_mask` and apply `.where(mask)` to every field before the correlation/RMSE; do not score each model on its own pairwise mask.",
        "`ocean_only=True` (the default) is correct here because WOA23 is the reference; report the cell counts the mask records alongside the metrics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "CMIP6 nitrate is stored per unit volume while WOA23 is per unit mass, so the nitrate values and hence the vertical gradient used to define the nitracline must be put in one concentration unit.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`no3` is archived in mol m-3 while WOA23 is µmol kg-1: they cannot be differenced or plotted on one scale until converted with the in-situ density (`compute_potential_density_anomaly` with `ref_pressure=None`), and the answer must state the density used (`attrs['density_assumption']`) — required for Figure 2's shared unit.",
        "The nitracline depth (depth of maximum gradient) is scale-invariant: take it from the native field with no conversion; a constant ρ cancels exactly, whereas an in-situ ρ would shift the depth slightly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The global and basin means depend on the basin partition, so the Pacific/Atlantic/Indian definitions and the exclusion of Southern and Arctic basins must be stated and applied consistently.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The Ofx `basin` field is not in the local archive: basin means use the WOA23 mask via `load_basin_mask`/`select_basin` with `include_marginal_seas=True` and `depth_dependent=False`, and the answer must state which mask was used and that Southern and Arctic are excluded.",
        "Marginal-sea folding changes basin means, so the choice must be reported with the numbers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "Each model's nitracline should be computed on its native grid, with regridding reserved for the WOA23-grid map and pattern comparison, because regridding changes masks and is not conservative.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute each model's global and basin mean nitracline on its own native grid with its own `areacello`; regrid to the WOA 1° grid only for the maps, pattern correlation and RMSE, stating the method ('conservative' going coarser, 'nearest_s2d' for the categorical basin mask).",
        "The nitracline is an extremum depth quantised by the vertical grid (the maximum can jump between levels where the profile is smooth); read the maps together with the gradient, and use `regrid_vertical` for the fixed-depth section of Figure 2 rather than selecting the nearest level."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "GFDL-ESM4 is supplied as gr (already regridded) while CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are gn, which affects which masks and comparisons are exact.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 output is `gr`, already remapped to 1° with its own land–sea mask, so its \"native-grid\" numbers are 1° numbers.",
        "CESM2 (100 km) and MPI-ESM1-2-LR (250 km) differ by about 2.5 in resolution; features narrower than the coarse grid are not comparable in amplitude."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "Land and below-sea-floor cells are marked with 1e20, and any read path that fails to mask them would corrupt the vertical-gradient search and basin/global means.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "xarray decodes 1e20 to NaN, and masks differ between variables of one model, so build each field's valid mask from the field itself and mask the weights to the same cells.",
        "A value near 1e20 in any output is an unmasked fill value, not a result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The nitracline from monthly-mean nitrate is a nonlinear diagnostic of averaged fields, so it need not equal the average of the online nitracline and this must be reflected in how the 1971–2000 climatology is built.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "f(monthly mean) ≠ mean of f: the nitracline of the 1971-2000 mean nitrate field is not the mean of the monthly nitraclines; state the order chosen, and average-first-then-diagnostic is the like-for-like choice against a WOA23 climatology.",
        "Average the monthly fields over 1971-2000 with `temporal_aggregate` (day weights in the model's calendar), not `compute_basic_stat(op='mean', dim='time')`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Global and basin mean nitracline depths require appropriate cell-area weighting and use of every ocean grid point in the region, not unweighted or subsampled averages.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Global and basin nitracline means must be area-weighted by `areacello` on the field's own grid (`compute_basic_stat` with `op='area_weighted_mean'`); an unweighted mean over latitude is wrong.",
        "The pattern correlation needs `weighting='area'` in `analyze_correlation`, and `compute_difference_metrics` (area-weighted by default) gives the RMSE and bias on the shared mask."
      ]
    }
